      "id": "TPD-01",
      "chapter": "normalization",
      "anchor": "normalization-transverse-period-decay",
      "title": "Integrating a translated coefficient leaves a power of the moved column",
      "hypotheses": "Discrete-series pair on signed unitary groups in dimensions n+1 and n with n≥3 and the stated large-gap interlacing hypotheses, opposite-sign separation 1000(n+1)³ and parameter bound B. The extension adds a positive unit coordinate. The translated lowest-type unit vector has ‖g₀‖F≤(8(n+1)B)^(10(n+1)).",
      "statement": "For model Haar μ₀ on the stabilizer, every translate restricted to the subgroup lies in L¹, and its absolute integral is ≤μ₀(N₁/₄)ℬ(1000)‖gz‖₂^(−2n−7).",
      "definitions": [
        "m=n+1, ℬ(C)=exp(Cm⁴log(8mB)), N₁/₄={h:‖h−1‖F≤1/4}.",
        "L=40m² powers are available, A=4n²+1 powers ensure convergence, and L−2A≥2n+7."
      ],
