    {
      "id": "TPD-03",
      "chapter": "normalization",
      "anchor": "normalization-transverse-period-class",
      "title": "The real product and the finite stabilizer volume give the bound for one rational class",
      "hypotheses": "A Hermitian extension by a positive unit line, f real places with the local bounds, an adelic Haar measure, a self-dual lattice containing z, a nonzero level ideal, and rational γ with zγ=γz. For the identity pairing use a level-invariant cusp vector as in the bottom period.",
      "statement": "For g=ι(x⁻¹)γ the absolute coefficient integral has weighted bound exp(fq)|c|. Here c=μf(K′)κ∏τcτ is the same scalar as in the identity contribution. The finite support Sg is empty or a single coset of K′.",
      "definitions": [
        "κ is the positive scalar comparing real Haar measure to the product over the f places. K′ is the preimage of the finite congruence subgroup.",
        "The geometric weight multiplies ‖Dτι(xτ⁻¹)zγ,τ‖₂ over the real places and raises the product to 2m+5."
      ],
